### Human intervention needed

The automated job failed in `explore/generate_tests()` while trying to create a test for the reporter-requested reflection access to `PrepareScriptFilenameConfigurationExtension.getUndoFilename()`.

Preserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-10323-fails-native-image-run-org.flywaydb-flyway-database-postgresql-11.12.0-b78f7bc4

Evidence:
- `fixTestNativeImageRun` completed successfully and generated metadata, so the initial metadata-repair stage was not the terminal failure.
- The dynamic-access report completed successfully and covered all 6 calls in `PostgreSQLCopyParsedStatement`, but it did not represent the reported access in the `flyway-core` class.
- All three generation attempts proposed configuring `flyway.prepare.undoFilename`, but each transcript says tests were not run. No test changes survived: metrics record 3 iterations, 0 generated LOC, and identical starting/ending commits.
- The setup preflight was also degraded after classifying the existing `docker run` test setup as unsafe, although setup and the initial fix still completed.

